<h2>Two kinds of arrest, two bodies of law</h2>
<div class="compare">
  <div class="col old">
    <h3>Arrest on accusation of an offence</h3>
    <p>Triggered by an FIR or complaint alleging a non-bailable offence. The person is an accused; the Constitution and the BNSS supply the full bail apparatus — anticipatory bail under Section 482, regular bail under Sections 480 and 483, default bail under Section 187.</p>
  </div>
